# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit a filled-in copy.
# Real values live in the private infrastructure repo; this file documents shape only.

# Postgres — data and the job queue. No Redis (see AGENTS.md tripwires).
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/motet_dev

# Which inference adapters to use: `fake` (default, deterministic, no network)
# or `real` (vendor calls — never in tests or CI).
MOTET_INFERENCE_MODE=fake

# Where the SPA is served from. The API and the SPA are two different hostnames in every
# deployed environment, so every call the web app makes is cross-origin — this is what the
# API's CORS policy is built from. Unset means no browser origin is allowed, which is
# right locally, where the Vite dev server proxies /v1 and the origin is shared.
# MOTET_APP_BASE_URL=

# Observability — the self-hosted obs stack, NOT GCP Cloud Logging (invariant 11).
# Every exporter no-ops when its variable is unset, so these are optional locally.
# An endpoint WITHOUT a credential is not "configured": obs rejects an unauthenticated
# export, so that combination buys a 401 per export rather than data. /healthz reports
# `telemetry_configured` false for it on purpose.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=motet-api
#
# The ingest credential, either way round. OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS is the standard
# variable and wins when both are set; OTEL_INGEST_TOKEN is the raw bearer, and is what
# a deployed environment actually gets — Secret Manager injects a secret under its own
# name, and the CI identity cannot read a value back in order to compose a header string.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=
# OTEL_INGEST_TOKEN=
#
# Exception tracking, under either of the two names the DSN travels as. GLITCHTIP_DSN is
# what the secret is called in Secret Manager.
# SENTRY_DSN_BACKEND=
# GLITCHTIP_DSN=

# --- LLM provider (motet_inference.llm) --------------------------------------
# OpenRouter is the provider Phase 1 ships. The key is injected from Secret Manager
# by the Cloud Run service definition (private infra repo); locally, put it here.
# Unset with MOTET_INFERENCE_MODE=real is a startup crash, on purpose.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Model selection is configuration, not code. One global default, one override per
# stage. Slugs are checked against the catalogue in motet_inference.llm.config at
# startup; verify one against OpenRouter's live list with bin/check-openrouter-models.
# MOTET_LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5
# MOTET_LLM_MODEL_DEDUP=
# MOTET_LLM_MODEL_SCRIPT=
# MOTET_LLM_MODEL_GROUNDING=

# Thinking depth: low | medium | high | xhigh | max, or `off` for no reasoning at all.
# Defaults are per stage — dedup=low (the volume line), script=high, grounding=max.
# MOTET_LLM_EFFORT=
# MOTET_LLM_EFFORT_DEDUP=
# MOTET_LLM_EFFORT_SCRIPT=
# MOTET_LLM_EFFORT_GROUNDING=

# Rarely needed. Provider follows MOTET_INFERENCE_MODE unless set explicitly; forcing
# `fake` while the mode is `real` runs real stages against fabricated completions, and
# logs a warning saying so.
# MOTET_LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
# MOTET_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# MOTET_LLM_ALLOW_UNLISTED_MODEL=false

# --- The single Phase 1 account ----------------------------------------------
# One shared bearer token guards every /v1 route. Phase 1 cuts signup and OAuth, so
# this is a lock on the door rather than an identity system. UNSET MEANS THE API IS
# OPEN — fine on a laptop, a mistake anywhere else; /healthz reports which it is.
# MOTET_API_TOKEN=

# --- Object storage (motet_storage) ------------------------------------------
# Where episode audio lives. `local` (default) writes files and lets the API serve
# them; `gcs` uploads to a bucket and hands out V4 signed URLs. The bucket name is
# injected by the service definition (private infra repo) and is not a fact this
# repo may know.
# MOTET_STORAGE_BACKEND=local
# MOTET_STORAGE_DIR=.motet-storage
# MOTET_AUDIO_BUCKET=
# MOTET_SIGNED_URL_TTL_SECONDS=3600

# --- The private RSS feed ----------------------------------------------------
# Absolute URLs in a feed cannot be relative, so the API needs to know its own origin.
# Left unset it derives one from the request, which is right locally and wrong behind
# a proxy that rewrites Host.
# MOTET_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
# MOTET_FEED_TITLE=Motet
# MOTET_FEED_DESCRIPTION=
# MOTET_FEED_AUTHOR=

# --- TTS (Cartesia Sonic) ----------------------------------------------------
# Sonic narrates; the realtime model converses (Phase 2). Every vendor-shaped fact is
# configuration so that a version or voice change is an environment change, not a PR.
# Both the key and the voice id are required when MOTET_INFERENCE_MODE=real — the
# worker refuses to start without them, on purpose.
# CARTESIA_API_KEY=
# MOTET_TTS_VOICE_ID=
# CARTESIA_VERSION=2024-06-10
# MOTET_TTS_MODEL=sonic-2
# MOTET_TTS_LANGUAGE=en
# MOTET_TTS_SAMPLE_RATE=44100
# MOTET_TTS_BIT_RATE=128000
# MOTET_TTS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=180

# --- Voice service (motet_voice, Phase 2) ------------------------------------
# Which arm serves sessions: `composed` (default — local VAD, OpenRouter, Cartesia)
# or `openai_realtime`. The barge-in harness ignores this and runs both.
# MOTET_VOICE_ARM=composed

# HMAC key for session tokens. There is no session store — the service is stateless so a
# WebSocket can land on any Cloud Run instance — so this key IS the session. Unset mints an
# ephemeral per-process secret and warns: fine on a laptop, and on a deployed service it
# means a token from one instance is rejected by the next. /healthz reports which it is.
# MOTET_VOICE_SESSION_SECRET=
# MOTET_VOICE_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=3600

# Where the platform tools (save_highlight, get_item_detail, mark_read, start_research)
# call Motet's own API. The voice service has NO database credential — invariant 2 — so
# this is the only way it reaches anything.
# MOTET_VOICE_API_BASE_URL=
# MOTET_VOICE_API_TOKEN=

# Bearer required to mint a voice session. UNSET MEANS ANYONE WHO CAN REACH THE SERVICE CAN
# OPEN ONE — and a session's tools call the API with the credential above, so an open
# StartSession is a path into the corpus rather than merely a way to spend budget. Fine on a
# laptop, a mistake anywhere else; /healthz reports which it is.
# MOTET_VOICE_START_SESSION_TOKEN=

# Conversation model for the composed arm. Falls back to MOTET_LLM_MODEL, then the seam's
# default. Reasoning is off for voice turns: a second of thinking is a second of somebody
# standing in the street.
# MOTET_VOICE_LLM_MODEL=

# NOT PROVISIONED. The OpenAI Realtime arm is built and dormant; setting this plus
# MOTET_VOICE_ARM=openai_realtime turns it on with no code change. Without it the arm's
# offline turn detection is an emulation of that vendor's documented server-VAD parameters,
# labelled as such in every report.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# MOTET_VOICE_OPENAI_REALTIME_MODEL=gpt-realtime

# NOT PROVISIONED. Wakes the start_research tool, which needs the Exa search vendor.
# EXA_API_KEY=
